", "No general-election polls, expert ratings, or market prices yet for 2028", "Open seat: term-limited incumbent removes any incumbency edge", "2026 Wisconsin headlines show a competitive, fluid political environment"], "rationale": "Wisconsin has decided recent presidential races by roughly a point and carries an even partisan lean, and with no polls, ratings, or prices yet available for the open 2028 contest, the even fundamentals stand. The wide uncertainty reflects how little direct evidence exists this early.", "watch": "The first credible general-election polls or expert ratings, and how the 2026 midterm aftermath settles in Wisconsin, could quickly tip the balance.", "confidence": "low", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Wisconsin remains one of the closest states in the country, with recent presidential margins decided by roughly a point or less and an even partisan lean. The 2028 race is an open contest with the incumbent term-limited, removing any incumbency advantage for either side. No general-election polls, expert ratings, or market prices are available yet, so the forecast rests on the state's fundamentals alone.\n\nHeadlines from 2026 point to a fluid Wisconsin scene: a tight governor's race, Democratic gains in the midterms, and early 2028 primary maneuvering on both sides. None of that yet establishes a clear edge in a presidential matchup. With the evidence evenly balanced, the race sits as a pure tossup, and the wide uncertainty reflects the absence of direct polling this far out.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.498, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.4982, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.5145, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.4971, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026